; The first six lines are clean: five resolve through the slot, one
; around it. Then the three that carry the story.
;
; `:radius` inside the slot is `unknown_key` and `:r` is missing — a
; global `circle` would have accepted `:radius` cleanly, which is what
; makes this pair the shadow's proof. `:rr` reports the same pair, and
; is where the LSP's quick fix has to draw its suggestion from the
; *local's* key set: resolved globally, the nearest key to `rr` is
; `radius`, a fix into a second diagnostic.
;
; `ghost` is `unknown_local_form` at the SLOT path, not `unknown_form` at
; the head — the slot is what the author has to look at.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code unknown_key :path [canvas shape circle radius])
  (diagnostic :code missing_required_key :path [canvas shape circle])
  (diagnostic :code unknown_key :path [canvas shape circle rr])
  (diagnostic :code missing_required_key :path [canvas shape circle])
  (diagnostic :code unknown_local_form :path [canvas shape]))
